<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Strike delays Gold Fields Nambia results.</title>
<headline>Strike delays Gold Fields Nambia results.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gold Fields Namibia Ltd said on Monday that results for the quarter ended September would be delayed due to disruption resulting from a recent six-week strike at its Tsumeb Corp Ltd.</p>
<p>It said results could be expected towards December.</p>
<p>Tsumeb Corp Ltd and the Mineworkers Union of Nambia (MUN) agreed last week on a 10.5 percent wage increase.</p>
<p>The strike is estimated to have cost N$50-100 million, Goldfields of Namibia said.</p>
<p>It reiterated that preliminary planning anticipated that after completion of the repairs to the smelting complex, production at its Tsumeb mines should commence in December.</p>
<p>A cash shortfall until sales resumed would be met from internal resources and an insurance claim related to the cost of repairs and loss of revenue had been lodged, Gold Fields said.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482-1003</p>
</text>
